,recipe
  ,title Cheeseburger Helper
  ,photo[cheeseburger-jar.jpg][A half-gallon jar of layered pasta and spices]
  ,yield 1 half-gallon or 1 half-pint (see tip)
  ,prep 5 min

  ,ingredients
    ,ul
      4 cups pasta (small shells or elbow macaroni)

      1 Tbs tomato powder

      2 Tbs beef bouillon

      ,frac[1/2] cup whole milk powder

      2 tsp dried minced garlic

      1 tsp smoked paprika

      1 tsp Italian seasoning

      ,frac[1/2] tsp salt

      ,frac[1/4] tsp pepper

  ,directions
    ,ol
      Place all ingredients into a half-gallon jar or other airtight
        container. ,em[Optional:] Vacuum seal.

  ,tip
    If you want to keep the pasta with all the other ingredients, you'll
    need a half-gallon jar. Alternatively, you can store the powdered
    ingredients and spices in a half-pint jar.

    This works well if your pasta is packaged in its ,strong[store-bought
    box]. See our ,link[https://example.com/jars][,em[jar] guide] for
    sizes ,image[lid.svg][lid icon] and footnote ,em[one][1]. Bare: ,link[https://example.com].
